NOTE:

Some people have reported problems when using optimizations larger than
-O2; typical symptoms are "prt-get install X" saying that a package is
installed while "prt-get update X" saying it's not, or "prt-get listinst"
printing just nothing.

If you experience strange effects, please try recompiling with 
   CXXFLAGS="-O2 -march=x86-64 -pipe"

BFSOS update dependency policy
------------------------------

Normal `prt-get update` and `prt-get sysup` transactions detect dependencies
that were added to already-installed packages and install those new hard
dependencies automatically.

For bootstrap transactions that must control dependency ordering explicitly,
BFSOS adds:

    prt-get update --no-new-deps <package>
    prt-get sysup --no-new-deps

The option reports newly required dependencies but intentionally does not
auto-install them for that update transaction. The explicitly requested update
is still attempted. `prt-get depinst` remains an explicit dependency-install
command and is not changed by this option.
